		<div class="post" id="post-1348015">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1348015)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1348015">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khym-chanur" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(163438); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=163438&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608367981" alt="Khym Chanur" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=163438)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khym-chanur" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(163438); return false;" >Khym Chanur</a></span> <span class="odate time_1326280135 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jan 2012 11:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1348015">
									

<blockquote>
<p>The ceiling of the storage facility, specifically the area directly over SCP-1050-1, must be shielded to block radio waves broadcast at an intensity of [REDACTED].</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not an electrical engineer, but even if the obelisk is transmitting the signal straight up I don't think that shielding only the ceiling immediately above it will block all of the radio signal.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1050 appears to be parts of an interstellar “early warning” system of unknown origin. Before the invention of more modern forms of rapid communication, some societies would light bonfires atop watchtowers, which would then be observed by the next watchtower, which would then light its own bonfire, and so on.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Nothing in the article suggests this to me. Now if the obelisk started sending a copy of an SCP-1050-3, <em>that</em> would suggest something like a series of bonfires.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1050-3 consists of a series of radio messages uncovered at different times by radio telescopes on four continents and in orbit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Might want to have a note on how embedded Foundation agents are preventing SETI from finding out about this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The numbers have been determined to be base-8 (Octal) representations of the forty base-10 (Decimal) integers in the obelisk message, preceded by another sixty integers following a similar pattern.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmmm. That would mean that the obelisks on other planets are using the length of Earth years to generate the numbers. It could be that when another obelisk is pointed towards our solar system it switches to using Earth years, but then wouldn't it also switch to base 10? And wouldn't the signal from <em>our</em> obelisk use numbers that would make sense to whoever is receiving it?</p>
<p>Also, repeating information that our obelisk already has isn't something that an early-warning system would do.</p>

							</div>

								
					
